</table></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="Ax19.SSx1.SSSx1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax19.SSx1.SSSx1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">In the subsequent iteration,based on performance across the past three iterations, we select the best-performing operators and meta-prompt modules to edit new prompt <math id="Ax19.SSx1.SSSx1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> . The ultimate objective is to minimize the overall loss, thereby maximizing the model’s overall performance metric.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">MSGD-RL Optimizer</h4>

<div id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As seen above, we need to initialize the selection probabilities for both the operators and the meta-prompt sections. To learn and recycle experience from past <span id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">transition matrix</span>, we define the procession of using operator to refine the section of prompt as a Markov Decision Process (MDP). The state <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the current prompt. The action <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is to choose operator <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to rewrite prompt section <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The reward <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by evaluating the predicted result against the ground truth. The <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the new prompt after rewriting. The <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is next action to refine the prompt. Specially, a function <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i,j}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i,j}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is designed to evaluate the value of using <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to optimize <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at the current time <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby supporting decision-making on the optimal action to take, as shown in Equation <a href="#Ax20.E6" title="In MSGD-RL Optimizer ‣ Case Study ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ PromptFlow: Training Prompts Like Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>,where <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{(}i,j)=Q_{L}(s_{i},a_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo></msub><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{(}i,j)=Q_{L}(s_{i},a_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-value for state <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and action <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> at Level <math id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax20.SSx1.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Ax20.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax20.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i,j}^{t}=\begin{bmatrix}Q_{(}0,0)&amp;Q(0,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(0,j)\\
Q(1,0)&amp;Q(1,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(1,j)\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
Q(i,0)&amp;Q(i,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(i,j)\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo></msub><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i,j}^{t}=\begin{bmatrix}Q_{(}0,0)&amp;Q(0,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(0,j)\\
Q(1,0)&amp;Q(1,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(1,j)\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
Q(i,0)&amp;Q(i,1)&amp;\cdots&amp;Q(i,j)\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
