<div id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Classification Task ‣ Experiment Results for Different Tasks ‣ Appendix D More Experiment Results ‣ PromptFlow: Training Prompts Like Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> also presents the results for the training and test sets of Qwen-max, respectively. The overall performance on Qwen-Max is inferior to that of QwQ-32b. The overall uplift on the training set is <math id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.25\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.25</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.25\%</annotation></semantics></math>. The improvement on Qwen-Max is better than that on Cluener, indicating that PromptFlow has an advantage in classification tasks. For the ”Horoscope” label, we observe a significant improvement as the number of training iterations increases, rising from <math id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="76.36\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>76.36</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">76.36\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.23\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.23</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.23\%</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstrating that the PromptFlow learned effectively. On the test set, the overall score improved by <math id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.45\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.45</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.45\%</annotation></semantics></math>, which is highly consistent with the results on the training set, confirming the effectiveness of our training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.SSx1.SSSx2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
